(wire (pts (xy 810.26 544.83) (xy 810.26 547.37)) (stroke (width 0) (type default)) (uuid c4a8c49b-c822-46ff-8cfd-417cb8bc0af0))
(label "-15V" (at 810.26 547.37 270) (fields_autoplaced) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right bottom)) (uuid 324cdaae-f492-4e91-b9f8-57b947104c89))
(text "POWER: external +/-15 V bench supply (Schottky reverse protection, ferrite filtering). L7805 -> +5 V (relays, DAC, Pico VSYS).\nMCP1700 -> +3V3, split by ferrites into +3V3A (ADC analog) and +3V3D (ADC digital, oscillator, logic pull-ups)." (at 20 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 4ae78785-5107-4b4d-aea5-b4dea2a89633))
(text "DRIVE INPUTS: BIAS/PULSE (DC) + AC PROBE (AC-coupled, JP3 = x1 or x0.1) + on-board bias DAC (via K21),\nsummed by U9 and re-inverted by U10:  VSET = V_bias + V_dac + k*V_ac." (at 20 128 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 762e96a3-e2fa-44c0-920b-8daa8e4ee7a1))
(text "BIAS DAC: DAC80501M (midscale at power-up) 0..5 V -> U11:  V_DAC_BIAS = 10.05 V - 4.02*V_DAC  (+10..-10 V, 0 V at midscale).\nConnected to the summer only when K21 closes (firmware sets range first)." (at 20 312 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6f27b06e-c2b4-46dc-95f7-5555ecf49338))
(text "CONTROL AMP U1: K7 DEV = follower (CE = VSET). K8 PSTAT (K7 off) = PI loop, V_RE = VSET. K9 RE_LOCAL ties RE sense to CE_INT.\nK10 CELL connects CE_INT to the CE BNC (open = cell disconnected). Cal loads (K11/K13) are T-switched: off -> mid node grounded by K12/K14 (NC)." (at 290 128 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 81b7cff7-003f-492e-9f27-2b258ca09863))
(text "RE: U2 electrometer follower, U3 guard driver (RE BNC shell + GUARD BNC), U7 RE_MON buffer (keeps monitor and nuller load off U2).\nV_OUT BNC: K19 (NC) = DC monitor V_RE/2 (U4); VMODE on -> K20 = AC monitor x10.1, AC-coupled ~100 Hz (U8)." (at 290 245 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid db1e7dfc-5d58-405d-b935-a3b8162b5050))
(text "NULLER (vector): U12 makes -V_RE. RV1 (0..-1) -> U13 -> 100p (+910p via K17) injects -jwC.V  (C null).\nRV2 (+1..-1) -> U14 -> 220n -> 20k (2k via K18) injects G null, AC-coupled (no DC into WE). K15/K16 (NULL_EN) connect to SUM_HI." (at 560 213 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid efed3a09-0492-49fc-a9a4-daaff6b10600))
(text "HIGH-GAIN TIA U5: WE = SUM_HI virtual ground. Ranges K1..K6 = 1k, 10k, 100k, 1M, 10M, 100M (relays on the output side).\n1 MHz C-V: use 1k and 10k only (100k and up roll off below 1 MHz). Q1/Q2 C-B junctions: low-leakage steering to the low-gain TIA U6." (at 560 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 7bac1b38-40e7-4093-81ae-ccd1ffc3f5c5))
(text "ADC: ADS131M04, 4 simultaneous channels, +/-1.2 V FS. Each input = 4.02k/1k divider (/5.02, +/-5 V -> +/-1.0 V) + 10 nF (~20 kHz).\nCH0 = V DC monitor, CH1 = I_HI, CH2 = I_LO, CH3 = AC V monitor. 8.192 MHz clock from X1." (at 20 400 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 47f44e50-0f55-470f-9142-22143f63bf6e))
(text "CONTROL: Pico 2 (socketed) drives CTL0..15 -> 2x TBD62783A high-side source drivers -> relay coils (off coils sit at 0 V).\nJ12 = CTL fallback header (Pico removed). 4.7k pulls set power-up state: ON = CTL3 (1M), CTL6 (DEV), CTL8 (RE_LOCAL)." (at 290 382 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5e4ebd32-edc7-4083-aaf9-a0cc3f35ca3f))
(text "Op-amp decoupling: one pair per op-amp, place at each op-amp supply pin." (at 580 512 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 71e3cec2-4e20-4097-a446-9288786342c7))
 (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1")))
)
